{{!--
    reference/nav - the API reference's section navigation: an operation filter over the
    whole API, and the tag list with the current tag's operations expanded.

    Rendered by views/layout/app.hbs into the secondary-nav column (the route sets
    `secondaryNav: 'reference/nav'`), so this partial owns only its inner content - the
    column's surface, border, width and sticky behavior belong to the layout. It emits
    no card or shadow on purpose: the column sits flush against the main sidebar and has
    to read as a continuation of it.

    The filter list is rendered server-side (all operations, hidden until the box has
    input) and narrowed by static/js/reference.js. There is no client-side index to
    fetch or build - filtering is plain DOM work over markup that is already there.

    A hit matches on more than it shows: `data-search` carries the operation id and every
    parameter and request-body property name as well. What is searchable is decided in one
    place, searchCorpus() in lib/api-reference/model.js - so "mailbox" or "mailMerge" finds
    the endpoints that accept them, not only the ones with the word in their path.

    Params (from the reference view context):
      nav         - tags with { name, slug, url, operationCount, active, operations[] }
      searchIndex - flat operation list backing the filter
--}}
<div class="flex flex-col gap-3 p-3">

    {{!-- Back to the reference home. Without it the only way out of a group page is the
          main side menu, which is easy to miss. --}}
    <a href="/admin/reference"
        class="flex items-center gap-2 rounded-field px-2 py-1.5 text-sm{{#if overviewActive}} bg-primary/10 text-primary font-semibold{{else}} hover:bg-base-200{{/if}}">
        <span class="icon-[tabler--home] size-4 shrink-0"></span>
        Overview
    </a>

    {{!-- Access-token status. Always a link to the control on the overview page, whatever
          the current state - the try-it panels on every group page depend on it, so it has
          to be reachable from all of them. The state text is repainted by
          static/js/reference.js from the token held for this tab. --}}
    <a href="/admin/reference/token"
        class="flex items-center justify-between gap-2 rounded-field px-2 py-1.5 text-sm{{#if tokenActive}} bg-primary/10 text-primary font-semibold{{else}} hover:bg-base-200{{/if}}">
        <span class="flex items-center gap-2">
            <span class="icon-[tabler--key] size-4 shrink-0"></span>
            Access token
        </span>
        <span id="ref-token-state" class="text-base-content/50 text-2xs">Not set</span>
    </a>

    {{> ui/search-input id="ref-filter" placeholder="Filter endpoints" shortcut="Ctrl K" shortcutMac="Cmd K" name="" value="" type="" class=""}}

    {{!-- Result count and key hints, shown only while the filter has input. The count is a
          live region so it is announced; the key hints are static decoration beside it. --}}
    <div id="ref-filter-hint" class="text-base-content/50 hidden items-center justify-between gap-2 px-2 text-2xs">
        <span role="status"></span>
        <span aria-hidden="true">Up/Down move, Enter open</span>
    </div>

    <ul id="ref-filter-results" class="flex flex-col gap-0.5 hidden">
        {{#each searchIndex}}
        <li class="ee-ref-hit" data-search="{{search}}">
            <a href="{{url}}" class="hover:bg-base-200 block rounded-field px-2 py-1.5">
                <span class="flex items-center gap-2">
                    <span class="text-{{methodVariant}} shrink-0 font-mono text-2xs font-semibold">{{method}}</span>
                    <span class="text-base-content/80 truncate text-xs">{{path}}</span>
                </span>
                {{#if summary}}<span class="text-base-content/50 block truncate ps-1 text-2xs">{{summary}}</span>{{/if}}
            </a>
        </li>
        {{/each}}
        <li id="ref-filter-empty" class="text-base-content/50 hidden px-2 py-2 text-xs">No matching endpoints</li>
    </ul>

    {{!-- Every group carries its operations, so the list of a group you are not on can be
          opened without loading its page. Below the layout's lg breakpoint the nav is a
          disclosure, and there static/js/reference.js turns a tap on a group row into opening
          that list instead of a page load - the chevron is the affordance for it. Which list
          is open is aria-expanded on the group row and nothing else: the attribute is the
          state, `max-lg:peer-aria-expanded:block` is the rendering.

          As a column it is not a disclosure at all - the active group's list is shown by
          lg:block and every other stays hidden, no matter what the reader last expanded on a
          narrow window. Without that, widening after collapsing the active group would leave
          the column with no list and no control to bring one back.

          Not FlyonUI's collapse or accordion, though both are in the bundle: HSCollapse
          animates an inline height that would fight lg:block (and strand a stale one when the
          viewport crosses lg), HSAccordion needs a <button> where these rows have to stay
          links above lg, and neither has any notion of a breakpoint - which is the whole
          problem here. --}}
    <ul id="ref-tag-list" class="flex flex-col gap-0.5">
        {{#each nav}}
        <li>
            <a href="{{url}}" aria-controls="ref-ops-{{slug}}" aria-expanded="{{#if active}}true{{else}}false{{/if}}"
                class="peer group flex items-center justify-between gap-2 rounded-field px-2 py-1.5 text-sm{{#if active}} bg-primary/10 text-primary font-semibold{{else}} hover:bg-base-200{{/if}}">
                <span class="truncate">{{name}}</span>
                <span class="flex shrink-0 items-center gap-1">
                    <span class="text-base-content/40 text-2xs">{{operationCount}}</span>
                    <span
                        class="icon-[tabler--chevron-down] text-base-content/40 size-3.5 transition-transform duration-200 group-aria-expanded:rotate-180 lg:hidden"></span>
                </span>
            </a>
            {{!-- ee-ref-op-nav marks the ACTIVE group's list only: it is the hook static/js/
                  reference.js scroll-spies on, and only that list holds in-page anchors to mark.
                  The current-state styling is written as aria-[current] variants here rather than
                  a rule in app.tailwind.css because a components-layer rule loses to the
                  text-base-content/70 utility on this same element - utilities are emitted later,
                  so the colour would silently not apply. Same utilities as the active tag entry
                  above, so the two levels read as one marker. --}}
            <ul id="ref-ops-{{slug}}"
                class="{{#if active}}ee-ref-op-nav lg:block {{/if}}border-base-content/10 my-1 ms-3 hidden border-s ps-2 max-lg:peer-aria-expanded:block">
                {{#each operations}}
                <li>
                    <a href="{{url}}"
                        class="text-base-content/70 hover:bg-base-200 hover:text-base-content aria-[current=location]:bg-primary/10 aria-[current=location]:text-primary aria-[current=location]:font-semibold block truncate rounded-field px-2 py-1 text-xs">{{summary}}</a>
                </li>
                {{/each}}
            </ul>
        </li>
        {{/each}}
    </ul>

</div>
